<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name "zsnapshot.manager">
<!ENTITY author "atsrxL">
<!ENTITY version "2026.08.20i">
<!ENTITY launch "Settings/ZFS-Snapshot-Manager">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atsrxL/unraid-zsnapshot-manager/main/plugin/zsnapshot.manager.plg">
<!ENTITY baseURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/atsrxL/unraid-zsnapshot-manager/2026.08.20i/src/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zsnapshot.manager">
]>
<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" launch="&launch;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" icon="camera" min="7.0.0" project="https://github.com/atsrxL/unraid-zsnapshot-manager" readme="https://github.com/atsrxL/unraid-zsnapshot-manager#readme">
<CHANGES>
### 2026.08.20i
- Added per-policy execution locking to prevent Cron and Run now races
- Fixed all-zero smart retention so it disables pruning instead of deleting all but the newest snapshot
- Preserved hidden/excluded policy targets during policy edits
- Simple clone names are now created inside the source pool, including pool-root snapshots
- Release source files are pinned to the matching version tag instead of mutable main
- Added GitHub Actions validation and automatic tagged Release creation

### 2026.08.20h
- Added optional multi-pool exclusion in Setting
- Excluded pools are hidden from Status, Snapshots and new Policy targets
- Existing snapshots and policies remain untouched

### 2026.08.20g
- Added a compact Status dashboard for pool capacity, snapshots, protection and policies
- Reworked Snapshots into a dataset navigator with one focused snapshot panel
- Moved the runtime activity log to the Setting tab
- Fixed tab order to Status, Snapshots, Schedules, Setting using native Unraid menu ranks

### 2026.08.20f
- Fixed Policy saves by replacing the removed JSON endpoint with Unraid's native command form channel
- Added a Settings tab with a persistent Show root datasets switch
- Collapsed empty datasets by default and added dataset filtering plus expand/collapse controls
- Added compact snapshot lists with an explicit Show all option
- Batched ZFS hold discovery to remove per-snapshot command calls

### 2026.08.20e
- Snapshot actions now use Unraid-native page POSTs and the verified command backend

### 2026.08.20d
- Added a guided Create snapshot policy button to the Snapshots home tab
- Added a three-step policy wizard and per-policy editing
- Each policy independently stores its target, frequency, retention, recursion and notification settings
- Fixed Run now on disabled policies so it actually performs the requested snapshot
- Added range-aware cron validation and atomic policy file writes

### 2026.08.20c
- Reworked ZFS mutations to use a dedicated shell backend like unriad-iscsi-manager
- Snapshot metadata is now written atomically with zfs snapshot -o instead of follow-up zfs set calls
- Removed the automatic page-level CSRF guard that could turn POST failures into blank pages
- Snapshot and schedule actions now use JSON endpoints and display errors inline
- Added hard operation timeouts so a stuck backend cannot hang the WebGUI indefinitely
- Removed per-snapshot metadata/type/mountpoint N+1 command calls
- Batched schedule retention metadata reads

### 2026.08.20b
- Fixed plugin updater to always replace RAM runtime files while preserving persistent schedules

### 2026.08.20a
- Fixed manual snapshot actions by moving them to a JSON/AJAX endpoint
- Moved ZFS Snapshot Manager to Settings > User Utilities
- Added smart retention: hourly, daily, monthly and yearly copies
- Smart retention keeps the newest snapshot in each time bucket and deduplicates overlaps
- Existing legacy Keep N policies remain backward compatible
- Simplified CSRF handling and improved action error reporting

### 2026.08.19b
- Fixed missing CSRF tokens on snapshot and schedule POST actions
- Moved plugin to Settings > System Settings
- Added one native xmenu entry with Snapshots and Schedules tabs
- Added guided schedule builder for minutes/hourly/daily/weekly/monthly/custom schedules
- Policy list continues to display standard 5-field cron expressions

### 2026.08.19a
- Initial test release
</CHANGES>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zsnapshot.manager
mkdir -p /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zsnapshot.manager/include
mkdir -p /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zsnapshot.manager/scripts
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;/include/lib.php">
<URL>&baseURL;/include/lib.php</URL>
</FILE>
<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;/scripts/zsm-manager.sh">
<URL>&baseURL;/scripts/zsm-manager.sh</URL>
</FILE>
<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;/scripts/zsm-scheduler">
<URL>&baseURL;/scripts/zsm-scheduler</URL>
</FILE>
<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;/scripts/zsm-policy-manager">
<URL>&baseURL;/scripts/zsm-policy-manager</URL>
</FILE>
<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;/scripts/zsm-settings-manager">
<URL>&baseURL;/scripts/zsm-settings-manager</URL>
</FILE>
<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;/ZFS-Snapshot-Manager.page">
<URL>&baseURL;/ZFS-Snapshot-Manager.page</URL>
</FILE>
<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;/ZFS-Status.page">
<URL>&baseURL;/ZFS-Status.page</URL>
</FILE>
<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;/ZFS-Snapshots.page">
<URL>&baseURL;/ZFS-Snapshots.page</URL>
</FILE>
<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;/ZFS-Schedules.page">
<URL>&baseURL;/ZFS-Schedules.page</URL>
</FILE>
<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/&name;/ZFS-Settings.page">
<URL>&baseURL;/ZFS-Settings.page</URL>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
set -e
mkdir -p /boot/config/plugins/zsnapshot.manager
[ -f /boot/config/plugins/zsnapshot.manager/schedules.json ] || printf '[]\n' > /boot/config/plugins/zsnapshot.manager/schedules.json
[ -f /boot/config/plugins/zsnapshot.manager/settings.cfg ] || printf 'SHOW_ROOT_DATASETS="yes"\nEXCLUDED_POOLS=""\n' > /boot/config/plugins/zsnapshot.manager/settings.cfg
chmod 0755 /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zsnapshot.manager/scripts/zsm-manager.sh
chmod 0755 /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zsnapshot.manager/scripts/zsm-scheduler
chmod 0755 /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zsnapshot.manager/scripts/zsm-policy-manager
chmod 0755 /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zsnapshot.manager/scripts/zsm-settings-manager
php -r "require '/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zsnapshot.manager/include/lib.php'; zsm_regenerate_cron();"
echo "ZFS Snapshot Manager 2026.08.20i installed"
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash" Method="remove">
<INLINE><![CDATA[
rm -rf /usr/local/emhttp/plugins/zsnapshot.manager
rm -f /boot/config/plugins/zsnapshot.manager/zsnapshot-manager.cron
/usr/local/sbin/update_cron >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
# schedules.json and settings.cfg are intentionally preserved for reinstall/recovery
]]></INLINE>
</FILE>
</PLUGIN>
